summary:
- topic: Administrator Contract Ratification
  text: The board unanimously ratified a three-year (2025-2028) collective bargaining
    agreement with the South Portland Administrators Association, marking the first
    of three major contracts to be settled.
- topic: Student and Staff Updates
  text: The student representative reported on back-to-school preparations, including
    a revised cell phone practice at the high school which prompted board discussion.
    The superintendent welcomed new staff and announced several resignations, including
    the Director of Food Services.
- topic: FY25 Budget Deficit
  text: The Finance Committee reported a current FY25 budget deficit of approximately
    $1.6 million. The new Director of Finance, Abigail Tchen, is analyzing the multi-year
    issue and awaiting a mid-September audit for clearer figures, while also exploring
    fundraising options like an educational foundation.
- topic: Board Leadership Election
  text: Following nominations for both Rosemary DeAngelos and Claire Holman for Vice
    Chair, the board debated the implications of the election, considering the upcoming
    turnover of four board seats. After a ballot vote, Rosemary DeAngelos was elected
    Vice Chair with a 4-2 majority.
- topic: Athletic Field Referendum
  text: The board approved revised language for the upcoming municipal referendum
    on the athletic fields. The changes, initiated by Board Member DeAngelos, clarify
    the choice between a 'natural grass' field and a 'synthetic turf' field to prevent
    voter confusion.
- topic: Board Communications
  text: Board members shared community updates, including reflections on the HiSET
    graduation, a 'Boys to Men' training, and the impressive quality of student art,
    highlighted by a story of a rediscovered piece from a 1984 SPHS graduate.
